---
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro'
import MotionCurve from '../../components/MotionCurve.astro'
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro'
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro'
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro'
import { group, type TokenDocument } from '../../lib/tokens.ts'

const springs = (prefix: string) =>
  group(prefix).map((doc: TokenDocument) => {
    const css = doc.light.css
    const spring = (doc.extensions as { spring?: { bounce: number } } | undefined)?.spring
    return {
      name: doc.cssVar.replace(/^--/, ''),
      duration: css[`${doc.cssVar}-duration`],
      easing: css[`${doc.cssVar}-easing`],
      bounce: spring?.bounce,
      description: doc.description,
    }
  })

const easings = group('motion.easing').map((doc) => ({
  name: doc.cssVar.replace(/^--/, ''),
  easing: doc.light.css[doc.cssVar],
  description: doc.description,
}))

const durations = group('motion.duration').map((doc) => ({
  name: doc.cssVar,
  value: doc.light.css[doc.cssVar],
  description: doc.description,
}))

const themeCss = `::view-transition-old(root),
::view-transition-new(root) {
  animation-duration: var(--sonar-motion-duration-theme);          /* 700ms */
  animation-timing-function: var(--sonar-motion-easing-crossfade); /* cubic-bezier(.4,0,.2,1) */
}

/* Without View Transitions: colors ease */
.sonar-theming, .sonar-theming * {
  transition: color var(--sonar-motion-duration-theme-fallback) ease,
              background-color var(--sonar-motion-duration-theme-fallback) ease !important;
}`

const themeJs = `function switchTheme(next) {
  const apply = () => (document.documentElement.dataset.theme = next)
  if (matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) return apply()
  if (document.startViewTransition) {
    // the knob slides first (200 ms), then the page cross-fades
    return setTimeout(() => document.startViewTransition(apply), 200)
  }
  document.documentElement.classList.add('sonar-theming')
  apply()
  setTimeout(() => document.documentElement.classList.remove('sonar-theming'), 300)
}`

const usage = `.accordion-panel {
  transition: height var(--sonar-motion-spatial-default-duration)
                     var(--sonar-motion-spatial-default-easing);
}

.menu {
  transition: opacity var(--sonar-motion-effects-fast-duration)
                      var(--sonar-motion-effects-fast-easing);
}`
---

<Docs title="Motion" description="Sonar-DB motion: springs defined by duration and bounce, generated as CSS easing curves, and when to use each.">
  <PageHeader
    title="Motion"
    lead="Short, decelerating, and without bounce by default. The interface is a working tool: motion explains what changed and gets out of the way. A small bounce is kept for two moments that deserve it."
  />

  <Section title="Springs" id="springs">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Springs are described as designers talk about them: a <strong>duration</strong>, the time the spring takes to
        settle within 0.2% of its target, and a <strong>bounce</strong>. The build turns each pair into
        a CSS <code>linear()</code> curve, so the motion runs like any transition, with no JavaScript.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Spatial</strong> springs move things: position, size, shape. <strong>Effects</strong> springs change how
        things look: opacity and color. Effects are quicker, because a fade that lags reads as slowness.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="curves">
      {springs('motion.spatial').map((spring) => <MotionCurve {...spring} />)}
      {springs('motion.effects').map((spring) => <MotionCurve {...spring} />)}
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Easing curves" id="easing">
    <p class="prose">Cubic curves for what is not a spring: leaving the screen, entering panels, the sidebar folding, the theme switch and cards changing columns.</p>
    <div class="curves">
      {easings.map((easing) => <MotionCurve {...easing} duration="400ms" />)}
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Durations" id="durations">
    <p class="prose">
      Fixed durations for the moments that are not a spring. Each is used with the easing named beside it in the
      guidelines below.
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap" data-scroll-region data-label="Motion durations">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Value</th><th scope="col">Use</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            durations.map(({ name, value, description }) => (
              <tr>
                <td><code>{name}</code></td>
                <td><code>{value}</code></td>
                <td>{description}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Theme switch" id="theme-switch">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Changing the theme is two steps. The switch’s knob slides first, in 200 ms on
        <code>--sonar-motion-easing-emphasized</code>. At 200 ms the whole page cross-fades into the new theme with a
        View Transition: 700 ms on <code>--sonar-motion-easing-crossfade</code>. Nothing changes color out of step,
        because the page fades as one picture.
      </p>
      <p>
        Browsers without View Transitions ease every color over 250 ms instead. With reduced motion requested, the
        theme changes at once.
      </p>
    </div>
    <CodeBlock code={themeCss} language="css" />
    <CodeBlock code={themeJs} language="js" />
  </Section>

  <Section title="In code" id="code">
    <p class="prose">Every spring is two custom properties, a duration and an easing, always used together.</p>
    <CodeBlock code={usage} language="css" />
  </Section>

  <Section title="Guidelines" id="guidelines">
    <ul class="prose">
      <li>
        Bounce only when a dragged card lands in its slot and when an action succeeds. Everywhere else, motion settles
        without overshoot.
      </li>
      <li>
        Side panels enter from 48 px in 420 ms with a fade, and leave by 28 px in 150 ms on the accelerate curve. On
        tablets the panel slides all the way in from the right edge on the default spatial spring (320 ms) and back out
        the same way, as <a href="/layout/navigation/#tablets">Navigation by device</a> shows. On phones the sheet rises
        in 420 ms (fade 200 ms) and drops in 220 ms.
      </li>
      <li>
        Menus open from 0.9 in 200 ms with a 138 ms fade, and close to 0.96 in 110 ms on
        <code>cubic-bezier(.3,0,.8,.15)</code>. The search list drops 4 px from 0.98 in 180 ms.
      </li>
      <li>
        Tooltips wait 300 ms, then grow from 0.96 in 140 ms; they leave with a 90 ms fade. The chart bubble only fades,
        in 200 ms.
      </li>
      <li>Hover and other state changes take 160 ms on <code>cubic-bezier(.23,1,.32,1)</code>.</li>
      <li>
        Editing the overview: a lifted card grows to 1.03 (200 ms) and rises to elevation 4; its height follows in
        320 ms. Dropped, it settles in 500 ms on the expressive spring. Neighbors and resizes move in 320 ms. When the
        column count changes, cards travel to their new places in 620 ms on <code>cubic-bezier(.2,0,0,1)</code>.
      </li>
      <li>Theme changes never move content: only the switch’s knob slides, then the page fades.</li>
      <li>
        With reduced motion requested, spatial movement is replaced by an immediate change; fades stay, shortened, to keep
        the change perceptible.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Section>
</Docs>

<style>
  .curves {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--sonar-space-16);
  }

  .table-wrap {
    min-width: 0;
    overflow: auto hidden;
    overscroll-behavior-x: contain;
    border-radius: var(--sonar-shape-corner-medium);
    background: var(--sonar-color-surface-card);
    box-shadow: var(--sonar-elevation-1);
  }

  .table-wrap table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font: var(--sonar-type-label-md);
    letter-spacing: var(--sonar-type-label-md-tracking);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .table-wrap caption {
    padding: var(--sonar-space-16) var(--sonar-space-16) var(--sonar-space-8);
    color: var(--sonar-color-text-strong);
    font: var(--sonar-type-title-md);
    letter-spacing: var(--sonar-type-title-md-tracking);
    text-align: left;
  }

  .table-wrap :is(th, td) {
    padding: var(--sonar-space-8) var(--sonar-space-16);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--sonar-color-divider);
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  .table-wrap thead th {
    color: var(--sonar-color-text-tertiary);
    font-weight: var(--sonar-font-weight-medium);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .table-wrap code {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
</style>
